<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="A" from="18" to="22" step="2"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="B" from="4" to="6" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="0.1" to="0.3" step="0.1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="m" from="24" to="36" step="6"/>
  <number name="d">$m/6</number>
  <number name="D">9*$m/6</number>

  <piecewiseFunction name="c" symbolic="false" styleNumber="1">
    <function domain="(-infinity,$m)">$A-$B*e^(-$k*x)</function>
    <function domain="[$m,infinity)">$A*e^(-$k/3*(x-$m))</function>
  </piecewiseFunction>

  <repeatForSequence from="0" to="8" valueName="n" name="heights">
    <round numDecimals="2">
      $$c(0+$n*$d)
    </round>
  </repeatForSequence>
  <sum name="heightsum" displayDecimals="5">$heights</sum>

</setup>

  <p>
    A person's rate of burning calories during a <m>$D</m>-minute workout is given the function <m>c(t)</m> whose output is measured in calories per minute at time <m>t</m> in minutes.  The following table shows some of the values of <m>c(t)</m>.
  </p>

      <tabular bottom="minor" top="minor">
        <row bottom="minor" halign="center">
          <cell><m>t</m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">0</number></m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">$d</number></m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">2*$d</number></m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">3*$d</number></m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">4*$d</number></m></cell>
        </row>
        <row halign="center">
          <cell><m>c(t)</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[1]</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[2]</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[3]</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[4]</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[5]</m></cell>
        </row>
      </tabular>

      <tabular bottom="minor" top="minor">
        <row bottom="minor" halign="center">
          <cell><m>t</m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">5*$d</number></m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">6*$d</number></m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">7*$d</number></m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">8*$d</number></m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">9*$d</number></m></cell>
        </row>
        <row halign="center">
          <cell><m>c(t)</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[6]</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[7]</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[8]</m></cell>
          <cell><m>$heights[9]</m></cell>
          <cell><m><number displayDecimals="2">$$c(9*$d)</number></m></cell>
        </row>
      </tabular>

<p>
  Our goal is to estimate and interpret the value of
  <me>
    \int_0^{$D} c(t) \, dt
  </me>
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Estimate the value of <m>\int_0^{$D} c(t) \, dt</m> using a left Riemann sum with <m>9</m> subintervals.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label><m>\int_0^{$D} c(t) \, dt \approx L_9 = </m></label>$d*$heightsum</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Complete the following sentence to explain the meaning of the definite integral.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since the units on <m>c(t)</m> are <choiceInput inline name="c1"><shortDescription>units on c of t</shortDescription>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>minutes</choice>
          <choice>calories</choice>
          <choice>calories per minute</choice>
          <choice>minutes per calorie</choice>
        </choiceInput>, and the units on <m>\Delta t</m> are <choiceInput inline name="c2"><shortDescription>units on delta t</shortDescription>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>minutes</choice>
          <choice>calories</choice>
          <choice>calories per minute</choice>
          <choice>minutes per calorie</choice>
        </choiceInput>, it follows that the units on definite integral <m>\int_0^{$D} c(t) \, dt</m> are <choiceInput inline name="c3"><shortDescription>units on the integral of c of t</shortDescription>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>minutes</choice>
          <choice>calories</choice>
          <choice>calories per minute</choice>
          <choice>minutes per calorie</choice>
        </choiceInput>, and hence the Riemann sum's value estimates <choiceInput inline name="c4"><shortDescription>what quantity the Riemann sum is an estimate of</shortDescription>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>the total time the workout took</choice>
          <choice>the average calories burned per minute in the workout</choice>
          <choice>the total calories burned during the workout</choice>
        </choiceInput>.
      </p>
      <p>
          <answer><award><when>
            $c1.selectedIndices=4 and $c2.selectedIndices=2 and $c3.selectedIndices=3 and
            $c4.selectedIndices=4
          </when></award></answer>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>